    "narrative": "For LawDog\u2019s July 5th slate, our top-tier plays are anchored by **Lawrence Butler** (71.26), **Bryson Stott** (71.23), and **Taylor Ward** (71.19). **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against P\u00e9rez, combining an advantageous park factor with a premium #4 spot in the order. **Bryson Stott** draws a favorable matchup against Avila, where the high xERA (5.01) creates significant run-production upside, while **Taylor Ward** remains our premier platoon play; his ability to capitalize on the Lodolo matchup, bolstered by an +18% SP skill boost and a +9% platoon advantage, keeps him as an elite start despite being listed in the OF4 slot.\n\nOur decision to bench **Gavin Sheets** (48.63) was the most difficult pivot of the day. While **Gavin Sheets** provides respectable power, he simply lacked the ceiling of our starters, particularly because the matchup against Sheehan (3.62 xERA) suppressed his scoring potential compared to the high-xERA matchups faced by **Jeremiah Jackson** or **Daulton Varsho**. Elsewhere, we are leaning heavily into the speed factor. We are tracking the stolen base potential for **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Drew Gilbert**, and **Daulton Varsho** against the slow deliveries of the opposing staff. **Jung Hoo Lee** in particular stands out with a 61.69 score, buoyed by a +14% park factor and the expectation that the team will prioritize base-stealing opportunities today.\n\nRegarding risks, the entire middle of our order faces a moderate test against Gordon, T. While **Luis Arraez**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Drew Gilbert** all benefit from the park factor, the proximity to a sub-4.00 xERA arm mandates careful monitoring. We are also proceeding without **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Yainer Diaz** due to their inactive status, necessitating that our starters maximize their efficiency to offset the absence of our core production. **Geraldo Perdomo** remains our utility anchor, holding a 59.18 score; while he faces a decent pitcher in Sproat, his presence is vital for maintaining our SB floor in a tight Roto race. **Cal Raleigh** (63.15) and **Jonathan Aranda** (67.67) should be considered high-probability starts, as their platoon-adjusted projections remain resilient against Yesavage and Lambert, respectively.",
